{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And they said: Has YHWH spoken only with Moses?</b> A limitation after a limitation is only for an inclusion, and the inclusion is: 'Has He not spoken with us too?' — before He spoke with Moses. How so? In Miriam's case, as they interpreted: she prophesied while she was still 'the sister of Aaron' and not the sister of Moses; and in Aaron's case — 'הנגלה נגליתי.'" "<b>And YHWH heard.</b> Even though they spoke in private, He exacted the affront."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:34.929492553Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}